# POLLY, the Sound page's preview: KNOB 1 (Sound) or PRESETS (the family) turned plays a short note in the new sound
# (300 ms, the middle of the instrument's range, straight into the synth on its channel: not out over MIDI), when it
# would not be heard otherwise: stopped, or playing while the instrument plays nothing. A fast turn: one note every
# 120 ms at most, the sound reached by then. None while recording or armed, none for the drums (no Sound knob).
# Pop: C1 (the piano) on channel 3, its range's middle G4 (67); C2 (no notes in Groove A) on channel 4; M1 on 7 (a
# melody's range is all: middle C, 60).
wait 300
tap EDIT
expect page 8
expect track 5
# ---- stopped: a turn, a note in the new sound; it ends by itself
hitreset
turn K1 1
wait 20
expect trk5_program 2
expect heard_ch3 67
expect ons_ch3 1
expect notes_out 0
expect voices >0
wait 1500
expect voices 0
# PRESETS: the next family (of eight), a note too
hitreset
turn PRESET 1
wait 20
expect trk5_program 9
expect ons_ch3 1
wait 400
# ---- a fast turn (10 detents, 40 ms apart): a note every 120 ms at most, not one a detent; the last sound wins
hitreset
turn K1 10 40
wait 400
expect ons_ch3 >2
expect ons_ch3 <6
# ---- armed (REC, stopped): no preview (the keys' notes are the take's)
tap REC
wait 50
expect recording 1
hitreset
wait 200
turn K1 1
wait 300
expect ons_ch3 0
tap REC
wait 50
expect recording 0
# ---- the drums: no Sound knob, no preview
turn ALGO -4
expect track 1
hitreset
turn K1 1
wait 300
expect ons_ch10 0
# ---- playing: C1 plays in Groove A (heard already); C2 has no notes there: its new sound previewed
turn ALGO 5
expect track 6
tap PLAY
wait 500
hitreset
turn K1 1
wait 20
expect heard_ch4 >0
expect ons_ch4 1
wait 300
tap PLAY
wait 300
# ---- a melody (M1), stopped: on its own channel
turn ALGO 3
expect lead_sel 1
hitreset
turn K1 1
wait 20
expect lsnd1_prog 82
expect lsnd1_chan 7
expect heard_ch7 60
expect ons_ch7 1
